english_question:
In the figure, there is a conical grain pile, whose front view is an equilateral triangle ABC with a side length of 6 m. A mouse is stealing grain at point P, the midpoint of the slant height AC, while a kitten is at point B. It needs to reach point P along the surface of the cone to catch the mouse. What is the shortest distance the kitten travels ( ) m?
A. 3
B. 3 \sqrt{3}
C. 3 \sqrt{5}
D. 4

In the figure, in parallelogram ABCD, AE bisects ∠BAD, intersecting BC at point E, and AB = AE. The extension of AB intersects the extension of DE at point F. Among the following conclusions: 
① △ABC ≌ △AED; 
② △ABE is an equilateral triangle; 
③ AD = AF; 
④ S_{△ABE} = S_{△CDE}; 
⑤ S_{△ABE} = S_{△CEF}. 
Which of the following is correct? ( )
A. ①②③
B. ①②④
C. ①②⑤
D. ①③④

In the circle O, chords AB and CD correspond to central angles ∠AOB and ∠COD respectively. If ∠AOB and ∠COD are complementary, and AB = 2, CD = 4, what is the radius of circle O?
Choices:
(A) √{3}
(B) 2
(C) √{5}
(D) 4
